course: dictionary
lesson: 2413
title: Cuttlefish: a master of disguise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out a new word by looking at the words around it. «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles, ten limbs in all.» The sentence tells you that arms and tentacles are both limbs, and that a cuttlefish has ten of them. A cuttlefish is a sea animal related to the squid and octopus.
explain: «Cuttlefish change colour and pattern in less than a second.» Pattern means the marks on the skin, so this is about how the animal looks. The science clue helps too: cuttlefish are masters of disguise, so they change how they look to blend in. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the dictionary gives two here: the animal itself, and what it does with its colour to hide or send messages. Ask: does the meaning fit? «The cuttlefish hid in the seaweed by changing its colour» still makes sense, so the meaning works.
fact: A cuttlefish is a sea animal related to the squid and octopus, but it is not a fish. It is a mollusc.
fact: A cuttlefish has eight arms, two long tentacles, a fin around its body and a hard flat shell inside called a cuttlebone.
fact: Cuttlefish change colour and pattern in a flash, to hide or to send messages.
fact: When in danger, cuttlefish squirt ink to escape, which is called cuttlefish ink.
fact: Cuttlebones wash up on beaches, and pet birds are given them to peck for calcium.
exercise: «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles.» Which animal is a cuttlefish related to? | *Squid | Crab | Whale | Seahorse
exercise: «Cuttlefish change colour and pattern in less than a second.» What is the main use of this? | To eat seaweed | *To hide or send messages | To swim faster | To keep warm
exercise: Which part of a cuttlefish is a hard flat shell inside its body? | Tentacle | Fin | Tail | *Cuttlebone
test: Why do cuttlefish squirt ink? | To keep warm | To write letters | *To escape from predators | To eat faster
test: Is a cuttlefish a fish? | *No, it is a mollusc | Yes, it is a fish with fins | No, it is a bird | Yes, it lives in rivers
exam: «In a test, cuttlefish waited for a shrimp they liked rather than take a less-liked crab at once.» What does «at once» mean here? | Never | Later on | After a long sleep | *Straight away
